-- title:
--   Two-pass SCC program, graph transpose, and component specifications
-- statement:
--   The concrete Kosaraju-style program calls DFS, constructs a transpose with separate adjacency rows, reverses the first finish-order prefix, and calls ordered DFS again. The transposition specification preserves vertex count, total arc occurrences, and every reversed arc multiplicity. The SCC postcondition requires a fresh component array and result object, labels in a contiguous range with every label used, and equal labels exactly when two original vertices are mutually reachable. The number of components is at most n and is zero exactly for an empty graph. All initial caller storage is preserved. Only the component fields of the returned DFSResult are specified by the SCC postcondition. Definitions fix the actual executed program; all associated theorems are open.
-- source:
--   CLRS, Introduction to Algorithms, fourth edition (MIT Press, 2022), Chapter 20, §20.5. https://mitpress.mit.edu/9780262046305/introduction-to-algorithms/ ; new arrays-of-arrays implementation compiled with Algo2Lean v0.1.4, https://www.algo2lean.com/versions/v0.1.4/ . Source filenames and full code are in the mission description.

